+# git_read checkpoint
+
+Date: 2026-10-26
+Status: Completed locally on 2026-10-27. Not pushed.
+The checkpoint sections below describe the earlier pause, not the current state.
+Task: Vikunja #1573, project #183 (`daimonos-agent`). The web task number is #225.
+Branch: `feat/1573-git-read`
+Repository: `/home/beardface/work/daimonos`
+ADR: `docs/adr/017-git-read-tool.md`
+
+## Completion
+
+- ADR-017 now includes its alternatives, consequences, confirmation checks, and verified anchors.
+- The final response cap covers failures as well as successes.
+- The tool also respects the shared response budget, without spilling large responses to disk.
+- Regression tests cover external git pointer files and missing tree objects.
+- The agent runtime test confirms that git_read runs while git remains blocked.
+- `cargo test`: 1993 passed, 0 failed, 10 ignored.
+- `python3 -m pytest tests/ -v`: 376 passed, 0 failed, 1 skipped.
+- Formatting, clippy, and whitespace checks passed.
+- The tests used the temporary dependencies described below. No crate dependency changed.
+- Policy findings are reproduced in `docs/security-reports/2026-10-27-delegated-tool-policy.md`.
+- Follow-up task #1574 tracks those findings. Their enforcement remains unchanged.
+- The MCP SDK omits root `additionalProperties`. The request parser still rejects unknown fields.
+- The shared `meetalix/tools/check_docs.py` checker is absent here. Anchors received direct source checks.
+- No newly unreachable code was identified.
+- The final comment on task #1573 records the completion commit.
+
+## User decisions
+
+- Implement a separate `git_read` tool. Leave `git` behavior unchanged.
+- The user approved ADR-017 and authorized local feature-branch commits.
+- Ignore submodules in `worktree_status`.
+- Reject alternate object stores outside the workspace.
+- Do not register the tool when git lacks `--no-lazy-fetch` support.
+- Omit a separate implementation plan for this personal project.
+- Do not add a crate dependency without confirmation.
+- Report batch and Starlark policy bypasses. Do not fix them in this change.
+- The user paused implementation for a commute. Preserve this checkpoint before shutdown.
+- No push or PR is authorized. Nothing was pushed during this work.
+
+## Implemented locally
+
+- All 11 operations exist in `src/plugins/git_read.rs`.
+- `src/plugins/git_read/runner.rs` owns process hardening and canonical confinement.
+- The runner disables optional locks, lazy fetching, external diffs, textconv, pagers, and fsmonitor.
+- It confines git directories and chained alternate stores to the workspace.
+- It removes inherited git environment prefixes and supplies a fixed environment overlay.
+- Results include repository paths and full commit SHAs. Failures use structured error kinds.
+- Caps live in `GitReadConfig` and `[git_read]` in `daimonos.default.toml`.
+- The shared plugin registry and MCP dispatcher expose the tool.
+- MCP dispatch uses the fixed workspace, not the mutable session cwd.
+- Generic CLI configuration cannot register the reserved `git_read` identity.
+- The agent policy test grants `git_read`, blocks `git`, and requires no interactive approval.
+- README, configuration docs, prompt descriptions, and the context map include the new tool.
+- No crate dependencies were added. `src/plugins/git.rs` is unchanged.
+
+## Verified results
+
+These results precede the last integration fixes. They do not certify the current tree.
+
+- Representative MCP tests passed for all 11 operations.
+- Eight focused Rust tests passed after the reserved-identity fix.
+- Rust tests exercise every operation against mutation snapshots and malicious repository configuration.
+- Snapshots include paths, sizes, content hashes, and mtimes for `.git` and the working tree.
+- Shallow and partial missing-object tests passed. A local listener received no connection.
+- The agent allowlist test passed.
+- `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed before the last integration changes.
+- `git diff --check` passed at shutdown preparation.
+
+## Last full-suite results
+
+- `cargo test --quiet`: 1973 passed, 14 failed, 10 ignored.
+- Twelve Rust failures came from missing `npm` and `shellcheck` programs.
+- Two Rust failures came from fixed parameter-description counts.
+- `python3 -m pytest tests/ -v`: 358 passed, 16 failed, 1 skipped.
+- Fifteen Python failures came from missing `npm` and `shellcheck` programs.
+- One Python failure came from inspecting a deliberately stripped MCP schema.
+- The Python log remains at `target/git-read-pytest.log`. It describes the earlier failed run.
+
+## Changes after those failures
+
+- Updated `DEFAULT_PARAMETER_DESCRIPTION_COUNT` from 140 to 156.
+- Changed the schema test to start MCP with `full_tool_schemas=true`.
+- Downloaded temporary npm 12.2.1 and ShellCheck 0.11.0 under `target/test-tools`.
+- Verified npm's published SHA-512 integrity and the ShellCheck release asset's SHA-256 digest.
+- Confirmed both temporary programs report their versions.
+- System packages did not change. Sudo requires a password.
+- The fixes and temporary test dependencies still need a full-suite rerun.
+
+## Resume
+
+1. Read AGENTS.md, task #1573, ADR-017, and the repository rules.
+2. Inspect the checkpoint commit and working-tree status before editing.
+3. Use the temporary test programs if this checkout still contains them:
+
+```bash
+export PATH="$PWD/target/test-tools/bin:$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH"
+cargo fmt -- --check
+cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings
+cargo test
+python3 -m pytest tests/ -v
+```
+
+4. Recreate temporary test dependencies if `target/` is absent. They are not committed.
+5. Fix the error-response byte cap. The current final size check covers successful results only.
+   Retain a regression test and review large-output behavior.
+6. Review missing-object classification, path handling, and all no-network guarantees.
+7. Check ADR completeness. Its current text lacks several standard ADR sections.
+8. Produce a runtime reproduction for the batch and Starlark policy findings.
+9. Record final results in Vikunja. Keep the task open until acceptance checks pass.
+10. Commit final changes locally. Do not push without authorization.
+
+## Policy audit still pending
+
+Source inspection found no inner `SafetyPolicy` check in batch or Starlark dispatch.
+The relevant symbols are `ops::dispatch_with_progress` and `script::dispatch_tool_by_name`.
+MCP mode also does not enforce the agent allowlist.
+A runtime reproduction and a separate report remain unfinished. Do not fix these paths here.
+
+## Shutdown state
